# The Setup screens, the key nation competitions, part 1: the international ones, Argentina, Australia, Belgium and Brazil (Setup.cpp, the block 0x830520 of the map; reader tel13, the screens round, 21/11/2026).
# Not screens: the competition creators of the key nation entries (G_LEAGUE_TABLE rows), called through
# KEY_NATION_RECORD_SETUP_FUNC by key_nation_create_all_comps 0x669180 (create_game) for the international rows and
# the nations with a selected league. Holds the mould (KeyNationComps, key_nation_create_comps, key_nation_check_comps) that tel13_3 and tel13_4 use; goes after tel13_1 (the KEY_NATION_RECORD_* names).
# Conventions checked in the disassembly and at the call site (0x6691a7: push ecx; call eax; add esp, 4): cdecl(entry)
# -> 1 or 0, ret 0; operator new 0x944cf1 and calloc 0x945501 cdecl; every constructor thiscall(this, year dword,
# competition record) ret 8 (checked: the first ret of each is ret 8); Date::Date 0x549f70 thiscall ret 0x10;
# Date::add_weeks 0x54c770 thiscall(date, out, 4) ret 8; key_nation_continent_has_selected_nation 0x6699d0 cdecl.
# Each routine was emulated (unicorn) from the original bytes with marked inputs (game year, start year, the nation's
# extra division bit, the continent answer) and the data of its KeyNationComps were taken from what it wrote: the
# entry's fields, the calloc arguments, each new size, constructor and its arguments and the slot.
# The year dword a constructor gets: the original pushes a dword whose high word is stack leftover (the year word
# was stored into a local); the copy zero-extends it (the constructors read the word). Brazil's is the dword of its
# date from the year on, as the original.
# Which run in the automatic career (ENG, auto_setup.cfg; once, in create_game): the international ones
# (world cup qualifying, other international, world club) and the five continental ones (they run in every career;
# each creates its cups only when a nation of its continent has a selected league: in the ENG career the European
# one with its 4 cups, the others with count 0). With the 8 leagues (ENG ESP ITA FRA BRA JPN AUS USA) also
# create_australian_comps and create_brazilian_comps, and the continental cups of those nations' continents.
# Argentina and Belgium only with their leagues chosen.
# DEFECTS of the original kept: the allocation messages of create_oceania_club_comps ("create_asian_club_comps()"),
# create_brazilian_comps and create_norwegian_comps (both "create_norwegian_comps()"), create_greek_comps
# ("create_german_comps()") and create_south_korean_comps, create_turkish_comps and create_welsh_comps
# ("create_spanish_comps()") name another routine; create_polish_comps and create_welsh_comps leave LEAGUE_COMP as it
# was; the world cup entry's season year is a fixed 1996 (0x7cc).
